rr software ticks (rr's tracee ABI version 1) for glibc's x86-64 assembly: the tick macros,
the entry ticks, and the loops that take more than a line of their own.

A compiler built for rr's software ticks predefines __RR_SOFTTICKS__ (the ABI version) and
ticks the code it compiles, at every function's entry and on every loop, so that no
instruction runs twice at the same pc and stack pointer without a tick in between; but not
hand-written assembly.  (Nor loops inside inline asm, which glibc's x86-64 C does not have.)

- sysdeps/x86_64/sysdep.h: RR_SOFTTICK, the ABI's x86-64 tick sequence exactly (rr
  recognizes ticks by their bytes; it clobbers the arithmetic flags only); RR_SOFTTICK_CF
  (r8), a tick that keeps CF in a dead 8-bit register; RR_SOFTTICK_ENTRY in ENTRY_P2ALIGN,
  after the endbr64: every function that ENTRY defines ticks first thing.
- sysdeps/x86_64/start.S: _start does not tick: in a static program it runs before anything
  has mapped the countdown's page (it maps it, glibc-100), and it runs once.
- The functions defined without ENTRY tick where they start: _dl_tlsdesc_return,
  _dl_tlsdesc_undefweak and _dl_tlsdesc_dynamic_* (the TLS descriptor convention lets them
  clobber the flags), _dl_runtime_resolve_* and _dl_runtime_profile_*, _dl_start_user
  (RTLD_START; its string is defined at the end of dl-machine.h, so that the asserts above it
  keep their line numbers), and the strcmp, strncmp, wcscmp, wcsncmp, strcasecmp_l and
  strncasecmp_l entries of strcmp-avx2.S, strcmp-evex.S and strcmp-sse4_2.S.
- add_n.S (__mpn_add_n, __mpn_sub_n): the carry is live round the loop:
  RR_SOFTTICK_CF (%al) before the jump back.  (The other mpn loops tick where no flag is
  live, glibc-102.)
- memmove-ssse3.S: the computed jumps into its 48 copy loops assume 64 (and 96) bytes per
  loop; with ticks every loop is 128 bytes long, and ticks at its top.
- __longjmp.S, setcontext.S and swapcontext.S: the shadow-stack loops, assembled with CET
  only, tick at their tops.

glibc-102-rr-softticks-loops.patch ticks all the other loops.  Without __RR_SOFTTICKS__ all
of this expands to nothing: the object code is the same as without the patches.

